1
00:00:00,023 --> 00:00:03,263
P’Mi can be herself anywhere.

2
00:00:03,300 --> 00:00:08,310
Even in how she sits.
She can lie down and stretch her legs out.
[BEING EMI REGARDLESS OF PLACES]

3
00:00:10,468 --> 00:00:11,321
Like this.

4
00:00:11,360 --> 00:00:13,204
I have an older sister
and a younger brother.

5
00:00:13,493 --> 00:00:14,139
Wow, that’s a big family.

6
00:00:14,161 --> 00:00:15,278
An older sister and a younger brother?

7
00:00:15,314 --> 00:00:17,331
Hey, same as me. We’re Wednesday children.

8
00:00:17,351 --> 00:00:19,241
You like finding similarities with others.

9
00:00:19,259 --> 00:00:21,848
-But we do have this similarity.
-True! Let me talk about this too.

10
00:00:21,877 --> 00:00:22,435
Fine, no similarities.

11
00:00:22,468 --> 00:00:24,194
I have 5 older sisters
and 16 younger brothers!

12
00:00:24,382 --> 00:00:25,016
Now we’re not the same.

13
00:00:25,074 --> 00:00:25,665
Here.

14
00:00:26,248 --> 00:00:26,780
One.

15
00:00:27,097 --> 00:00:27,608
Two.

16
00:00:27,890 --> 00:00:29,745
You need to make the train sound, toot toot~

17
00:00:30,365 --> 00:00:31,309
Toot toot~

18
00:00:32,717 --> 00:00:33,797
Chugga chugga chugga chugga…

19
00:00:34,620 --> 00:00:36,334
[SWEETNESS OVERLOADED]

20
00:00:36,334 --> 00:00:37,188
This is the trick I always use.
[SWEETNESS OVERLOADED]

21
00:00:37,284 --> 00:00:41,848
Yes, use this trick if your kid refuses to eat.

22
00:00:41,871 --> 00:00:42,746
It really works.

23
00:00:42,774 --> 00:00:45,133
-It works on adults too.
-It does.

24
00:01:00,610 --> 00:01:03,331
Tay New Meal Date Special

25
00:01:06,567 --> 00:01:07,751
Thank you Canon.

26
00:01:07,842 --> 00:01:10,328
Choose a quality printer,
choose Canon MEGA TANK

27
00:01:10,466 --> 00:01:11,524
Never Lets You Down

28
00:01:12,274 --> 00:01:14,499
We’re going to Ari.

29
00:01:14,533 --> 00:01:15,007
Who knows the way?
[GOING TO ARI]

30
00:01:15,022 --> 00:01:15,952
No introduction needed at all?
[GOING TO ARI]

31
00:01:15,968 --> 00:01:17,736
No need. Our show is real.

32
00:01:17,952 --> 00:01:19,321
It’s Gen Z style. We focus on authenticity.

33
00:01:19,788 --> 00:01:22,231
If you introduce the show,
that’s Boomer style.

34
00:01:22,231 --> 00:01:23,210
[PROPER INTRO = BOOMER ENERGY]

35
00:01:23,281 --> 00:01:24,503
Hey, are you hungry?

36
00:01:24,560 --> 00:01:25,318
I’ve got some food supplies here.

37
00:01:25,349 --> 00:01:26,195
You can’t be serious.

38
00:01:26,365 --> 00:01:28,394
-I've got fruits. I'm the banana presenter.
-You can just do whatever here?

39
00:01:28,463 --> 00:01:30,131
I can’t have any other fruit
because I’m the banana presenter.

40
00:01:30,150 --> 00:01:32,050
I might get criticized for not
having both hands on the wheel.

41
00:01:32,082 --> 00:01:33,103
Fine, I’ll peel it for you.

42
00:01:34,109 --> 00:01:35,601
Are you really the banana presenter?

43
00:01:35,700 --> 00:01:36,402
I’m joking.

44
00:01:37,248 --> 00:01:38,903
-Ughhhhh.
-I’m shipping this so hard.

45
00:01:38,924 --> 00:01:39,256
[EMI DOESN'T LIKE BANANAS.]

46
00:01:39,256 --> 00:01:41,631
The banana is #*@!
[EMI DOESN'T LIKE BANANAS.]

47
00:01:43,560 --> 00:01:45,592
-P’Mi is afraid of bananas.
-Let’s talk about her fun fact.

48
00:01:45,622 --> 00:01:47,188
Emi hates bananas, right?

49
00:01:47,210 --> 00:01:48,757
I hate bananas the most.
[BANANA HATER]

50
00:01:48,757 --> 00:01:49,105
[BANANA HATER]

51
00:01:49,105 --> 00:01:50,453
I actually can’t stand the smell
right now.
[BANANA HATER]

52
00:01:50,468 --> 00:01:50,933
[CAN'T EVEN STAND THE SMELL]

53
00:01:50,933 --> 00:01:52,438
-You can smell it?
-Yes.
[CAN'T EVEN STAND THE SMELL]

54
00:01:52,438 --> 00:01:52,454
[CAN'T EVEN STAND THE SMELL]

55
00:01:52,454 --> 00:01:53,106
You can smell it already?
[CAN'T EVEN STAND THE SMELL]

56
00:01:53,168 --> 00:01:53,813
Yeah.

57
00:01:54,115 --> 00:01:55,499
Tay, why did you peel it?

58
00:01:55,694 --> 00:01:57,254
I thought you didn’t like the texture.

59
00:01:57,278 --> 00:01:58,189
You don’t like the smell either?

60
00:01:58,220 --> 00:01:59,930
-All of it.
-She has trauma with bananas.

61
00:01:59,940 --> 00:02:01,410
I have trauma with them.
[BANANA TRAUMA]

62
00:02:01,605 --> 00:02:03,349
All kinds?

63
00:02:03,400 --> 00:02:04,189
The soft ones.

64
00:02:04,645 --> 00:02:07,816
-Oh, so you’re not afraid of hard bananas.
-What about green bananas, the raw ones?

65
00:02:08,213 --> 00:02:08,840
-Those too.
-I just don’t eat them.

66
00:02:08,860 --> 00:02:11,804
But I’m okay with banana chips
and deep-fried banana fritters.

67
00:02:12,280 --> 00:02:13,650
Did the show already start?

68
00:02:13,674 --> 00:02:14,317
[GUESTS ARE CONFUSED.]

69
00:02:14,317 --> 00:02:15,610
I don’t think it has.
[GUESTS ARE CONFUSED.]

70
00:02:16,475 --> 00:02:17,884
But you’re eating
a banana while filming?

71
00:02:18,294 --> 00:02:19,568
What’s my TikTok name?

72
00:02:19,617 --> 00:02:20,794
Taytadaotiktok (TayTa, TikTok star)

73
00:02:20,908 --> 00:02:23,084
-Being a TikTok star means I start trends.
-Free spirit?

74
00:02:23,173 --> 00:02:23,776
Free spirit.

75
00:02:23,848 --> 00:02:27,804
Someone who names their TikTok
“TikTok star” feels kind of Boomer though.

76
00:02:29,480 --> 00:02:32,985
Bonnie, you look like someone
who reads manga.

77
00:02:33,008 --> 00:02:33,709
Do you read manga?

78
00:02:33,813 --> 00:02:34,299
No.

79
00:02:34,324 --> 00:02:36,176
You look like a gamer too.

80
00:02:36,205 --> 00:02:37,945
But I watch anime.

81
00:02:37,970 --> 00:02:39,750
Yeah, you look like that type.
[AN ANIME FAN]

82
00:02:40,154 --> 00:02:40,994
Which one?

83
00:02:41,788 --> 00:02:42,317
Oh!

84
00:02:42,367 --> 00:02:43,390
Oh, there’s a camera here.

85
00:02:43,411 --> 00:02:44,056
You just noticed?

86
00:02:44,080 --> 00:02:45,005
Yes.

87
00:02:45,152 --> 00:02:46,823
I kept looking at that camera.

88
00:02:46,823 --> 00:02:48,250
[RIGHT IN FRONT OF YOU]

89
00:02:48,310 --> 00:02:51,531
That’s why I heard them saying,
“They might not see us. Let’s squeeze in.”

90
00:02:51,548 --> 00:02:53,694
Yeah, that’s why I’m sitting like this.

91
00:02:53,826 --> 00:02:54,865
Hi.

92
00:02:54,945 --> 00:02:55,654
Hi.

93
00:02:55,687 --> 00:02:57,694
They might think we're subtly
leaning toward each other.

94
00:02:58,096 --> 00:02:59,577
We were just worried we’d be out of frame.

95
00:02:59,681 --> 00:03:02,099
♪ You’re more than the word “love” ♪

96
00:03:02,174 --> 00:03:05,591
♪ What you are to me, my love ♪

97
00:03:05,862 --> 00:03:08,613
♪ Just a glance, just a touch ♪

98
00:03:08,668 --> 00:03:12,349
Do you know your MBTI?

99
00:03:12,410 --> 00:03:14,654
Mine is kind of flexible.
[FLEXIBLE MBTI]

100
00:03:14,677 --> 00:03:15,710
It changes every day?
[FLEXIBLE MBTI]

101
00:03:15,740 --> 00:03:17,423
Yes, it does. But I’m a P.

102
00:03:17,444 --> 00:03:17,851
[ENDING WITH P]

103
00:03:17,851 --> 00:03:19,790
Does yours end with P?
[ENDING WITH P]

104
00:03:19,805 --> 00:03:21,152
Same as mine.

105
00:03:21,626 --> 00:03:23,388
I knew it from how you eat.

106
00:03:23,417 --> 00:03:25,309
No, I don’t think that’s related.

107
00:03:25,693 --> 00:03:27,288
I’m just trying to find a connection.

108
00:03:27,342 --> 00:03:31,197
As for Emi, you seem like someone
like Force?

109
00:03:31,234 --> 00:03:32,706
Actually, P’Mi is E.

110
00:03:32,737 --> 00:03:33,011
[BEGINNING WITH E]

111
00:03:33,011 --> 00:03:34,030
Yes, she does seem like one.
[BEGINNING WITH E]

112
00:03:34,130 --> 00:03:36,979
-Someone who doesn’t talk much.
-Yeah.

113
00:03:37,899 --> 00:03:38,948
Let’s explain.

114
00:03:39,110 --> 00:03:39,819
Not talking—

115
00:03:39,875 --> 00:03:42,094
No need to talk about everything.

116
00:03:42,112 --> 00:03:43,768
Yeah, that.
People often misunderstand that.

117
00:03:43,802 --> 00:03:47,450
P’Mi can be herself anywhere.

118
00:03:47,470 --> 00:03:49,579
Even in how she sits.
[BEING EMI REGARDLESS OF PLACES]

119
00:03:49,645 --> 00:03:53,057
She can lie down and stretch her legs out.

120
00:03:53,500 --> 00:03:55,245
I’m not embarrassed by that kind of thing.

121
00:03:55,277 --> 00:03:57,832
But I’m not very chatty.

122
00:03:57,890 --> 00:03:59,906
I’m just a bit quiet.

123
00:04:00,013 --> 00:04:01,804
She makes any place she goes
feel like home.

124
00:04:02,881 --> 00:04:03,434
Really?

125
00:04:03,487 --> 00:04:05,099
Really. I call that her ability.

126
00:04:05,240 --> 00:04:07,914
As for me, when I go somewhere new,
I sit properly and feel tense.

127
00:04:07,937 --> 00:04:08,899
But she can just…

128
00:04:10,244 --> 00:04:11,186
She goes like this.

129
00:04:11,244 --> 00:04:15,385
-As if she were at home, on her own bed.
-Yes, that’s true.

130
00:04:15,474 --> 00:04:18,391
If you’re like what Bonnie said,

131
00:04:18,441 --> 00:04:21,915
what about going to
a completely new place like Fashion Week?

132
00:04:21,942 --> 00:04:22,847
You’ll meet new people there.

133
00:04:22,881 --> 00:04:23,826
Are you excited?

134
00:04:23,869 --> 00:04:25,100
It depends on the situation.

135
00:04:25,121 --> 00:04:26,565
As for Fashion Week—

136
00:04:26,592 --> 00:04:27,594
The recent one.

137
00:04:27,640 --> 00:04:28,958
I’ve been practicing since I was young.

138
00:04:28,982 --> 00:04:29,314
[BEEN PRACTICING]

139
00:04:29,314 --> 00:04:30,560
Practicing what?
[BEEN PRACTICING]

140
00:04:30,560 --> 00:04:30,605
[BEEN PRACTICING]

141
00:04:30,605 --> 00:04:31,579
No, not like that.
[BEEN PRACTICING]

142
00:04:31,604 --> 00:04:34,401
-I mean I’ve been watching it
since I was young.
-You’re well prepared.

143
00:04:34,493 --> 00:04:37,720
Ah, so you already know what to do.

144
00:04:37,755 --> 00:04:40,099
So I feel like
I’ve been there for a while.

145
00:04:40,148 --> 00:04:41,002
Really?

146
00:04:41,437 --> 00:04:43,485
-Yes.
-Emi in Paris, right?

147
00:04:43,511 --> 00:04:45,002
-No, I mean—
-That’s Emily.

148
00:04:46,204 --> 00:04:47,577
Not that kind of feeling.

149
00:04:47,601 --> 00:04:48,050
I mean…

150
00:04:48,081 --> 00:04:51,808
for Thai shows,
I like watching Bangkok Gossip,

151
00:04:51,828 --> 00:04:53,974
the high-class gossip and interview show.

152
00:04:54,056 --> 00:04:54,745
Have you watched it?

153
00:04:54,780 --> 00:04:56,197
What about Fashion Week?

154
00:04:56,226 --> 00:04:58,952
-I mean I don’t feel tense or awkward.
-I used to watch the F Fashion channel.

155
00:04:59,029 --> 00:05:00,724
-Yeah, I watched F TV.
-What is it?

156
00:05:01,380 --> 00:05:02,133
It’s a fashion channel.

157
00:05:02,260 --> 00:05:02,734
[TOTAL CLUELESS]

158
00:05:02,734 --> 00:05:03,530
It’s similar to how media
film fashion shows these days.
[TOTAL CLUELESS]

159
00:05:03,530 --> 00:05:05,868
It’s similar to how media
film fashion shows these days.

160
00:05:05,949 --> 00:05:08,850
Another thing is, I have this mindset that
there’s nothing I can do.

161
00:05:09,426 --> 00:05:10,647
“I can do it or I can’t?”

162
00:05:10,671 --> 00:05:11,528
Nothing I can do.

163
00:05:11,588 --> 00:05:13,066
That letting-go feeling.

164
00:05:13,090 --> 00:05:14,672
-Yes.
-That’s our motto now.

165
00:05:14,690 --> 00:05:17,324
-“Nothing we can do.”
-“Nothing we can do.”

166
00:05:17,343 --> 00:05:18,131
You just have to let go.

167
00:05:18,148 --> 00:05:19,508
Like it’s not under our control.

168
00:05:19,540 --> 00:05:23,026
Yes, we can’t control it, so we let it go.

169
00:05:23,053 --> 00:05:23,995
Just let it be.

170
00:05:24,450 --> 00:05:25,543
You can hang out with New.
He’s like this too.

171
00:05:25,565 --> 00:05:29,271
-Yes, we’re the same.
-Yes, New has that same mindset.

172
00:05:29,290 --> 00:05:31,314
-Are you like me, obsessive?
-Yes!

173
00:05:31,660 --> 00:05:33,471
[TAY'S FOUND HIS LONG LOST SIBLING.]

174
00:05:33,471 --> 00:05:34,150
Ask New.
[TAY'S FOUND HIS LONG LOST SIBLING.]

175
00:05:34,730 --> 00:05:36,782
He’s always like, “Hey, that’s enough.”

176
00:05:37,020 --> 00:05:40,038
He keeps reading scripts, again and again.

177
00:05:40,063 --> 00:05:41,973
-I overthink repeatedly.
-Overthinking, overdoing.

178
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:46,533
The thing is, I feel guilty for not reading
while you keep reading.

179
00:05:46,614 --> 00:05:49,102
I can’t help worrying about
what’s next and what to do next.

180
00:05:49,124 --> 00:05:52,872
Yes, I feel like I need to know
what I have to do.

181
00:05:52,899 --> 00:05:55,462
I don’t want to just jump
into the water without knowing.

182
00:05:55,540 --> 00:05:56,899
Yes, but if I ask P’Mi,

183
00:05:57,091 --> 00:05:58,804
she’ll say,
“Let’s see when tomorrow comes.”

184
00:05:58,817 --> 00:06:00,674
Let’s talk about it tomorrow.
Don’t think about it now.

185
00:06:00,694 --> 00:06:02,201
We like to just jump in.

186
00:06:02,222 --> 00:06:03,463
Yes, and it’s not boring.

187
00:06:03,560 --> 00:06:06,659
That’s why he likes those thrill rides.

188
00:06:06,684 --> 00:06:07,419
I hate them.

189
00:06:07,441 --> 00:06:08,514
Same.

190
00:06:08,823 --> 00:06:10,352
-But I don’t like those rides either.
-I’m scared of them.

191
00:06:10,520 --> 00:06:11,585
But New really enjoys them.

192
00:06:11,620 --> 00:06:14,037
I don’t like things
that are beyond my control.

193
00:06:14,062 --> 00:06:15,549
I don’t like flying on planes either.

194
00:06:16,425 --> 00:06:19,097
Yeah, especially
when there’s news about it.

195
00:06:19,247 --> 00:06:19,951
So scary.

196
00:06:19,970 --> 00:06:21,382
-You know, I’m overly scared.
-Bonnie’s hands are sweaty.

197
00:06:21,453 --> 00:06:22,866
My hands become sweaty
when there’s turbulence.

198
00:06:22,903 --> 00:06:25,202
If there’s turbulence, I sit like this.

199
00:06:25,462 --> 00:06:27,331
While New thinks
he’s on an amusement park ride.

200
00:06:27,900 --> 00:06:30,282
“Are you crazy? I’m terrified.”

201
00:06:30,350 --> 00:06:31,411
But he’s having fun.

202
00:06:31,441 --> 00:06:32,131
Is P’New an S?

203
00:06:32,150 --> 00:06:33,902
New is S. I’m N.

204
00:06:33,922 --> 00:06:35,211
-What am I?
-You’re S.

205
00:06:35,350 --> 00:06:37,485
-Which letter is S?
-It’s the second letter in MBTI.

206
00:06:37,534 --> 00:06:39,693
We’re N, so we imagine things.

207
00:06:39,739 --> 00:06:42,071
Yes, we tend to have wild thoughts.

208
00:06:42,477 --> 00:06:44,189
But most pairs are like this.

209
00:06:44,234 --> 00:06:46,011
Yes, opposite in some aspects.

210
00:06:46,045 --> 00:06:47,167
-Yes.
-To make it through together?

211
00:06:47,192 --> 00:06:50,293
But there are pairs
that aren’t that different,

212
00:06:50,318 --> 00:06:52,112
like First and Khaotung.

213
00:06:52,137 --> 00:06:52,826
Are they really similar?

214
00:06:52,857 --> 00:06:56,884
Not completely,
but not as contrasting as us.

215
00:06:57,831 --> 00:06:58,811
Like Off and Gun, they’re more like us.

216
00:06:58,834 --> 00:07:01,177
But it’s good to have an opposite side
to balance things a bit.

217
00:07:01,244 --> 00:07:03,998
No, we’re not completely opposite.

218
00:07:04,065 --> 00:07:05,597
We’re opposite, but on a straight line.

219
00:07:05,597 --> 00:07:06,610
[STRAIGHT LINE?]

220
00:07:07,640 --> 00:07:08,468
Like hairstyles?

221
00:07:08,626 --> 00:07:09,920
Straight hair?

222
00:07:09,940 --> 00:07:13,324
I mean the opposite like this.

223
00:07:15,280 --> 00:07:15,986
[IT HAS TO BE THIS KIND OF OPPOSITE.]

224
00:07:15,986 --> 00:07:17,768
We complement each other, right?
[IT HAS TO BE THIS KIND OF OPPOSITE.]

225
00:07:17,854 --> 00:07:23,143
I mean, to survive in this industry,
we need both.

226
00:07:23,794 --> 00:07:24,616
Yin and yang.

227
00:07:24,653 --> 00:07:25,628
Yes, exactly.

228
00:07:25,850 --> 00:07:27,623
Is there a camera at the back
for P’Tay too?

229
00:07:28,245 --> 00:07:29,680
Ahhh!

230
00:07:29,986 --> 00:07:31,208
He’s really like P’Mi.

231
00:07:31,502 --> 00:07:32,927
So similar.

232
00:07:32,977 --> 00:07:34,555
P’Mi likes to randomly shout sounds
out of nowhere.

233
00:07:34,580 --> 00:07:34,834
[P'MI LIKES TO MAKE SOUNDS.]

234
00:07:34,834 --> 00:07:36,767
Just out of nowhere.
[P'MI LIKES TO MAKE SOUNDS.]

235
00:07:36,816 --> 00:07:37,502
Yes.

236
00:07:37,860 --> 00:07:40,090
She’s always like, “Oi,” “Ugh.”

237
00:07:40,106 --> 00:07:41,028
So free.

238
00:07:41,065 --> 00:07:43,291
You’re really like P’Mi, P’New.
[ANOTHER P'MI RIGHT HERE]

239
00:07:43,291 --> 00:07:43,328
[ANOTHER P'MI RIGHT HERE]

240
00:07:43,328 --> 00:07:44,281
You really are.
[ANOTHER P'MI RIGHT HERE]

241
00:07:44,985 --> 00:07:45,936
I’ve got goosebumps.

242
00:07:46,810 --> 00:07:47,896
You really got goosebumps?

243
00:07:52,037 --> 00:07:53,060
We’re going to a restaurant
called Ong Tong.

244
00:07:53,114 --> 00:07:54,177
Have you been there before?
[ONG TONG KHAO SOI]

245
00:07:54,180 --> 00:07:55,854
Never.
[ONG TONG KHAO SOI]

246
00:07:55,875 --> 00:07:57,650
From the name, what kind of food
do you think they serve?

247
00:07:58,350 --> 00:08:00,001
Northeastern food?

248
00:08:00,051 --> 00:08:01,524
It’s something crowded.

249
00:08:01,714 --> 00:08:02,568
Why?

250
00:08:02,597 --> 00:08:03,505
Because it’s an ensemble.

251
00:08:05,440 --> 00:08:06,230
[SHY BY HIS OWN JOKE]

252
00:08:06,266 --> 00:08:07,668
I don’t get it.

253
00:08:10,365 --> 00:08:12,628
Ong Tong serves northern food.

254
00:08:12,837 --> 00:08:13,623
Can you eat that?

255
00:08:13,710 --> 00:08:14,749
Yes, I even love it.

256
00:08:14,813 --> 00:08:15,687
Bonnie likes northern food.

257
00:08:15,745 --> 00:08:18,088
Do either of you eat healthy food?

258
00:08:18,140 --> 00:08:19,934
-Emi.
-I do, but only sometimes.

259
00:08:19,952 --> 00:08:21,545
She ordered delivery on set every day.

260
00:08:22,260 --> 00:08:23,579
I was really plump back then.

261
00:08:23,605 --> 00:08:25,651
-When I wore an A-line skirt.
-I’ve never seen you plump.

262
00:08:25,690 --> 00:08:27,397
I could barely breathe
in that tight skirt.

263
00:08:27,431 --> 00:08:29,736
That’s when I realized I was fat.
[CAN’T BREATH IN THAT A-LINE SKIRT]

264
00:08:29,767 --> 00:08:30,628
What about you?

265
00:08:30,730 --> 00:08:33,127
I eased up on dieting.

266
00:08:33,160 --> 00:08:34,868
During breaks, he went golfing.

267
00:08:34,960 --> 00:08:35,968
“I’ll be back. I’m going to play golf.”

268
00:08:35,992 --> 00:08:36,549
Seriously?
[SO CHILL]

269
00:08:36,579 --> 00:08:38,330
“I'm going to practice my putting
for a bit. I’ll be back soon.”
[SO CHILL]

270
00:08:38,364 --> 00:08:39,321
Your life is so flexible.

271
00:08:39,431 --> 00:08:41,051
Can you drop me at the hospital
before Ong Tong?

272
00:08:41,082 --> 00:08:42,500
I think I’ve strained my neck.

273
00:08:43,688 --> 00:08:44,800
Is your neck starting to hurt?

274
00:08:44,960 --> 00:08:46,170
STARTING POINT: GMMTV >

275
00:08:46,200 --> 00:08:48,150
1st STOP: ONG TONG KHAOSOI ARI

276
00:08:54,050 --> 00:08:57,530
Yeah. We’re at Ong Tong now.

277
00:08:57,602 --> 00:08:59,330
-What I ate and really liked here—
-This one’s really good.

278
00:08:59,360 --> 00:09:00,522
2 fresh coconut juice, please.

279
00:09:00,571 --> 00:09:02,040
Can I get coconut juice too?

280
00:09:02,059 --> 00:09:03,281
3 coconut juices, please.

281
00:09:03,426 --> 00:09:04,317
Would you like one too, Emi?

282
00:09:04,411 --> 00:09:05,629
Orange juice for me.

283
00:09:06,914 --> 00:09:08,296
-Typical juice for female leads?
-Female lead.

284
00:09:08,580 --> 00:09:10,102
I'm gonna have Nam Ngiao.
(Northern Spicy Pork Soup)

285
00:09:10,186 --> 00:09:11,100
Nam Ngiao for me too.

286
00:09:11,117 --> 00:09:12,328
2 Nam Ngiao, please.

287
00:09:12,754 --> 00:09:13,675
2?

288
00:09:13,802 --> 00:09:14,844
One each for me and her.

289
00:09:15,031 --> 00:09:16,050
Aren’t you getting anything else?

290
00:09:16,133 --> 00:09:16,745
Other dishes too.

291
00:09:16,774 --> 00:09:18,247
But this is my main dish
and I won’t share it.

292
00:09:18,990 --> 00:09:20,240
It’s exclusively mine.

293
00:09:20,262 --> 00:09:22,096
Are you food possessive too?

294
00:09:22,127 --> 00:09:23,522
Yes, but I don’t make it obvious—

295
00:09:23,545 --> 00:09:24,494
Oi!

296
00:09:26,257 --> 00:09:27,888
Take it easy, Mi. Take it easy.

297
00:09:28,090 --> 00:09:29,469
Jin too.

298
00:09:29,573 --> 00:09:30,075
No “Jin.”

299
00:09:30,105 --> 00:09:31,595
I'm not gonna "Jin" you two. (Ship/Meat)

300
00:09:31,801 --> 00:09:33,281
I mean pork.

301
00:09:34,943 --> 00:09:36,302
You keep on with the “Jin” nonstop.

302
00:09:36,703 --> 00:09:37,902
We’re at Ong Tong,

303
00:09:37,928 --> 00:09:40,385
and the ruler of this place is here
to personally welcome us.

304
00:09:40,416 --> 00:09:42,146
P'Top honored us by being here.

305
00:09:42,171 --> 00:09:43,247
Hello, P’Top.

306
00:09:45,050 --> 00:09:46,348
Get up. Let P’Top sit here.

307
00:09:48,410 --> 00:09:49,774
How bossy you are.

308
00:09:50,310 --> 00:09:51,891
Is this the original Ong Tong restaurant?

309
00:09:51,917 --> 00:09:52,691
It’s the first branch.

310
00:09:52,715 --> 00:09:54,548
Is this the first branch in the world
or just in Bangkok?
[ONG TONG KHAO SOI, ORIGINAL BRANCH]

311
00:09:54,568 --> 00:09:55,268
In the world.

312
00:09:55,293 --> 00:09:56,477
What about the one in Chiang Mai?

313
00:09:56,503 --> 00:09:57,651
That’s another restaurant.

314
00:09:57,677 --> 00:09:58,948
It’s called Ong Tong Boat Noodles.

315
00:09:58,982 --> 00:10:01,063
The recipes are from your family, right?

316
00:10:01,097 --> 00:10:03,085
Yes, they’re from my grandmother.

317
00:10:03,189 --> 00:10:05,548
What was the concept
when you opened this restaurant?

318
00:10:05,640 --> 00:10:08,511
I already had that noodle restaurant
in Chiang Mai,

319
00:10:08,537 --> 00:10:10,964
and I wanted to expand.

320
00:10:11,014 --> 00:10:14,321
So I thought about what to sell
if I opened in Bangkok.

321
00:10:14,346 --> 00:10:16,472
There are already so many
strong noodle places here.

322
00:10:16,502 --> 00:10:17,780
So I felt—

323
00:10:17,976 --> 00:10:19,288
You want to do something differently.

324
00:10:19,311 --> 00:10:21,045
I also had Khao Soi on the menu,

325
00:10:21,367 --> 00:10:23,742
so I decided to focus on Khao Soi here
and make it the brand of this place.

326
00:10:23,765 --> 00:10:28,389
You even developed special dishes,
like the one I used to have here,

327
00:10:28,410 --> 00:10:29,622
-the dried Khao Soi.
-Dried Khao Soi.

328
00:10:29,638 --> 00:10:32,952
-You created that dish yourself.
-Yes, I created the sauce myself.

329
00:10:32,974 --> 00:10:37,373
I used a stir-fry technique
to bring out the wok aroma.
[STIR-FRIED WOK AROMA]

330
00:10:37,400 --> 00:10:39,108
Yes, I love that stir-fried aroma in food.
[STIR-FRIED WOK AROMA]

331
00:10:39,133 --> 00:10:40,760
-Do you plan to expand further?
-My restaurant?

332
00:10:40,783 --> 00:10:44,659
Actually, I already have
7 Ong Tong Khao Soi branches.

333
00:10:44,684 --> 00:10:45,242
That’s a lot.

334
00:10:45,278 --> 00:10:48,272
Are there challenges in
managing multiple branches?

335
00:10:48,358 --> 00:10:49,594
There are always issues.

336
00:10:49,616 --> 00:10:52,835
Operations get more complicated

337
00:10:52,865 --> 00:10:55,274
as the number of branches increases,
and I have to maintain consistent standards.

338
00:10:55,385 --> 00:10:57,327
And we also have a central kitchen system.
[MAINTAINING STANDARDS]

339
00:10:57,350 --> 00:11:02,988
What about paperwork, invoices,
orders from different suppliers?

340
00:11:03,189 --> 00:11:04,262
Is there a lot of documentation?

341
00:11:04,293 --> 00:11:05,297
A lot. A lot.
[SO MUCH PAPERWORK]

342
00:11:05,322 --> 00:11:06,700
It piles up like a mountain.
[SO MUCH PAPERWORK]

343
00:11:06,770 --> 00:11:08,851
Even internally,
we print documents every day.

344
00:11:08,942 --> 00:11:09,520
We totally understand.

345
00:11:09,542 --> 00:11:13,457
Running a business involves many things,
especially backend work and paperwork.

346
00:11:13,494 --> 00:11:15,214
You really have to print a lot of documents.

347
00:11:15,250 --> 00:11:16,802
So I’d like to introduce this.
[TAY PROUDLY PRESENTS…]

348
00:11:25,825 --> 00:11:29,229
Welcome to the Tay–New Festival.

349
00:11:29,600 --> 00:11:32,755
Introducing the Canon MegaTank GX4070,

350
00:11:32,842 --> 00:11:35,146
a multifunction printer for businesses.

351
00:11:35,343 --> 00:11:37,352
Printing documents is super convenient

352
00:11:37,485 --> 00:11:41,404
because this is an all-in-one printer
with Wi-Fi and fax.

353
00:11:41,560 --> 00:11:43,002
Perfect for businesses.

354
00:11:43,130 --> 00:11:47,900
Print, scan, copy, or fax,
you can do all that in one machine.

355
00:11:49,134 --> 00:11:49,797
That’s right.

356
00:11:49,915 --> 00:11:54,407
And this little guy comes with
an ADF automatic document feeder.

357
00:11:54,524 --> 00:11:58,414
Plus, it has multiple connection options—

358
00:11:58,564 --> 00:12:01,277
including Android and Wi-Fi.
[iOS, ANDROID, Wi-Fi CONNECTIONS]

359
00:12:01,280 --> 00:12:02,007
Most importantly,
[iOS, ANDROID, Wi-Fi CONNECTIONS]

360
