tap “Scan,”

377
00:12:38,914 --> 00:12:39,964
and there you go.

378
00:12:40,097 --> 00:12:40,811
Wow.

379
00:12:42,444 --> 00:12:45,998
Choose a quality printer,
choose Canon MEGA TANK

380
00:12:46,157 --> 00:12:47,103
Never Lets You Down

381
00:12:47,260 --> 00:12:48,085
What do you think, P’Top?

382
00:12:48,108 --> 00:12:49,422
It’s very interesting.

383
00:12:49,462 --> 00:12:51,491
I already have a lot of
documents to print,

384
00:12:51,509 --> 00:12:54,804
so having a good printer
would really help reduce costs.

385
00:12:56,105 --> 00:13:00,669
And even color printing is easy,
with great quality too.

386
00:13:01,560 --> 00:13:02,970
[CHICKEN KHAO SOI]

387
00:13:03,280 --> 00:13:04,930
[CRAB PASTE + STICKY RICE]

388
00:13:05,220 --> 00:13:06,390
[DEEP-FRIED PORK NECK
WITH GREEN CHILLI DIP]

389
00:13:06,700 --> 00:13:08,330
[NAM NGIAO WITH RICE VERMICELLI]

390
00:13:09,368 --> 00:13:10,330
Let’s dig in.

391
00:13:10,360 --> 00:13:11,487
They all look mouthwatering.

392
00:13:11,521 --> 00:13:12,371
Let’s start.

393
00:13:17,426 --> 00:13:19,050
Does Hang-Le Curry mean it hesitates?

394
00:13:19,118 --> 00:13:20,108
That’s “Lang-le.”

395
00:13:20,832 --> 00:13:22,232
I’m glad you corrected my word pun.

396
00:13:22,346 --> 00:13:23,871
You’re quiet now.
Pay attention to the guests.

397
00:13:23,899 --> 00:13:24,607
You do the talk too.

398
00:13:24,641 --> 00:13:26,035
He’s in his own world now.

399
00:13:26,077 --> 00:13:27,002
What did she say?

400
00:13:27,296 --> 00:13:27,992
Do that pun again.

401
00:13:28,019 --> 00:13:29,004
No, I'd rather not.

402
00:13:34,325 --> 00:13:36,854
The Nam Ngiao here is really friendly.

403
00:13:36,870 --> 00:13:37,837
Yes, it is.
[FRIENDLY DISH]

404
00:13:37,860 --> 00:13:39,160
It’s mild and tasty.
[FRIENDLY DISH]

405
00:13:39,340 --> 00:13:40,703
I want to be friends with it.

406
00:13:41,120 --> 00:13:44,069
For anyone who thinks
Nam Ngiao is hard to enjoy,

407
00:13:44,120 --> 00:13:45,484
I want you to give it a try.
It's a delicious dish.

408
00:13:45,500 --> 00:13:47,063
You just need to be open-minded.
[GIVE NAM NGIAO A TRY]

409
00:13:47,063 --> 00:13:47,281
[GIVE NAM NGIAO A TRY]

410
00:13:47,281 --> 00:13:49,894
Bonnie, can you describe
and promote this dish?
[GIVE NAM NGIAO A TRY]

411
00:13:49,965 --> 00:13:52,768
It’s mildly spicy,

412
00:13:53,114 --> 00:13:55,054
just a hint of chili in the soup.

413
00:13:55,630 --> 00:13:56,641
There's a slight tanginess,

414
00:13:56,660 --> 00:13:58,845
and when you add some lime juice,
you really get that citrus aroma.

415
00:13:58,917 --> 00:14:01,696
And the soup has a light tomato aroma.

416
00:14:01,718 --> 00:14:02,591
Yes, exactly.

417
00:14:02,645 --> 00:14:06,497
I like stir-fried noodles like
pad thai or Pad See Ew,
[STIR-FRIED DRIED KHAO SOI WITH BEEF]

418
00:14:06,500 --> 00:14:08,208
and this dish gives a similar feeling.

419
00:14:08,810 --> 00:14:09,936
Go ahead.

420
00:14:10,149 --> 00:14:11,447
P’New already tried it.

421
00:14:15,853 --> 00:14:17,865
-It tastes like Moo Stay.
-It has herbs.

422
00:14:17,893 --> 00:14:19,471
Yeah, I get the herbal aroma.
[HERBAL DISH]

423
00:14:19,499 --> 00:14:21,589
The sauce coats every single noodle.

424
00:14:21,817 --> 00:14:24,077
It has this mild, mellow scent and…

425
00:14:24,127 --> 00:14:26,202
-Wok aroma.
-Yes, wok aroma.

426
00:14:28,290 --> 00:14:30,096
Have you tried this chicken?
The fried chicken is really good.

427
00:14:30,120 --> 00:14:31,395
Yes, it is.
[FRIED CHICKEN’S SO GOOD!]

428
00:14:31,499 --> 00:14:32,555
I only noticed when it was almost gone.

429
00:14:32,580 --> 00:14:34,727
-Me too. I only had the first piece.
-One more fried chicken, please.

430
00:14:34,758 --> 00:14:37,325
Normally, I don’t order fried chicken
when I eat here.
[FRIED CHICKEN WITH GREEN CHILLI DIP]

431
00:14:37,352 --> 00:14:38,511
But it turned out to be really good.
[FRIED CHICKEN WITH GREEN CHILLI DIP]

432
00:14:38,700 --> 00:14:40,202
It goes really well with the chili dip.

433
00:14:40,339 --> 00:14:43,170
We’re testing New’s MC skills
for a food show.

434
00:14:43,605 --> 00:14:45,331
Please introduce this Khantok set.

435
00:14:45,351 --> 00:14:46,724
Can you tell us what’s included in this set?

436
00:14:46,770 --> 00:14:49,200
This greeny thing is definitely
Nam Prik Noom (Green Chilli Dip).

437
00:14:49,414 --> 00:14:52,469
And the red one is Nam Prik Ong
(Spicy Pork and Tomato Dip).

438
00:14:52,714 --> 00:14:53,902
And this is Pork Crackling.

439
00:14:54,291 --> 00:14:55,380
What kind?

440
00:14:55,408 --> 00:14:56,551
The one with a thick fat layer.

441
00:14:57,340 --> 00:14:59,157
-And this is tomato and—
-As thick as his sin.

442
00:14:59,235 --> 00:15:00,238
Coriander?

443
00:15:00,265 --> 00:15:00,937
Correct.

444
00:15:00,968 --> 00:15:03,598
-Is this Moo Yor (pressed pork)?
-Yes, Moo Yor.

445
00:15:03,937 --> 00:15:05,684
-Did you "Yor" me yet? (praise)
-You're awesome.

446
00:15:05,722 --> 00:15:07,602
♪ I just love you this way ♪

447
00:15:11,720 --> 00:15:13,705
This one is Sai Oua
(Northern Herb Pork Sausage)

448
00:15:13,968 --> 00:15:15,002
And the last one.

449
00:15:15,044 --> 00:15:15,774
"Jor" what?

450
00:15:15,810 --> 00:15:16,557
Joraka.

451
00:15:16,580 --> 00:15:17,370
It's Jor Phak (Boiled vegetables).

452
00:15:17,391 --> 00:15:18,657
You're Joraka. (Villain in a Thai literature)

453
00:15:19,647 --> 00:15:21,280
You're Joraka Longsong.

454
00:15:27,010 --> 00:15:29,200
How was filming the series with P’Mi?

455
00:15:30,226 --> 00:15:31,321
It went smoothly.

456
00:15:31,370 --> 00:15:37,472
Actually, the series itself
has a very dark and difficult script,

457
00:15:37,487 --> 00:15:38,214
and it really drained us.

458
00:15:38,242 --> 00:15:40,567
So the atmosphere on set
was kept relaxed instead,

459
00:15:40,591 --> 00:15:42,897
so we wouldn’t be too stressed.
[CHILL ATMOSPHERE]

460
00:15:43,176 --> 00:15:45,029
Why did you suddenly decide to go to
Mon Kuwera at that time?

461
00:15:45,056 --> 00:15:46,125
Have you been there?

462
00:15:46,284 --> 00:15:47,201
Yes.

463
00:15:48,324 --> 00:15:50,998
Want to guess who invited whom?

464
00:15:51,051 --> 00:15:52,051
Who initiated it?

465
00:15:52,094 --> 00:15:53,131
-Her.
-Who?

466
00:15:53,400 --> 00:15:54,192
Emi?

467
00:15:54,320 --> 00:15:55,638
-I can’t remember.
-P’Mi did.

468
00:15:55,834 --> 00:15:59,302
But I’m the type
who’s afraid to invite people.

469
00:15:59,608 --> 00:16:00,269
That’s not true.

470
00:16:00,331 --> 00:16:02,398
I mean, I try.

471
00:16:02,610 --> 00:16:04,287
But normally, I don’t like
asking someone to go with me.

472
00:16:04,310 --> 00:16:06,896
I’m afraid of getting a no.

473
00:16:07,582 --> 00:16:09,902
In this case, Bonnie and I
were working together,

474
00:16:10,060 --> 00:16:11,081
so I gave it a try.

475
00:16:11,114 --> 00:16:13,632
But I was worried
she might not want to go.

476
00:16:13,662 --> 00:16:17,194
Originally, I planned to go by myself.

477
00:16:17,325 --> 00:16:19,611
Then again, she might wonder
why I didn’t invite her.

478
00:16:19,982 --> 00:16:22,469
-I see. I get it.
-I already planned to go there.

479
00:16:22,715 --> 00:16:24,720
-So you asked her just in case.
-Yes, I asked her,

480
00:16:24,760 --> 00:16:26,811
-and it turned out she wanted to go too.
-Oh, so it was just the two of you?

481
00:16:26,900 --> 00:16:27,573
Yes.

482
00:16:27,604 --> 00:16:28,995
My mom went with us.

483
00:16:29,025 --> 00:16:29,928
With Bonnie’s mom too.

484
00:16:29,948 --> 00:16:33,168
So you believe in spiritual manifestation?

485
00:16:33,271 --> 00:16:34,585
I do, from the start.

486
00:16:34,767 --> 00:16:36,872
P’Mi always asks me to do
spiritual manifestation practices.

487
00:16:36,943 --> 00:16:40,997
The first thing we talked about was Ganesha.

488
00:16:41,028 --> 00:16:45,044
-That temple is actually beautiful,
clean, and well organized.
-Yes, very peaceful.

489
00:16:45,109 --> 00:16:46,441
It has the same vibe as Japanese temples.

490
00:16:46,474 --> 00:16:47,358
When I entered, I felt cold.

491
00:16:47,380 --> 00:16:50,299
-They manage the place really well.
-Yes, it was cold.

492
00:16:50,325 --> 00:16:51,622
Of course it’s cold. It’s Chiang Mai.

493
00:16:51,648 --> 00:16:54,217
No, I meant the atmosphere
feels calm and cooling.

494
00:16:54,240 --> 00:16:55,642
There’s a nice breeze and lots of trees.

495
00:16:55,670 --> 00:16:56,637
They’re just joking.

496
00:16:56,820 --> 00:16:58,410
Oh, you’ve never been there?
[NEW'S NEVER BEEN THERE YET.]

497
00:16:58,430 --> 00:16:59,943
-He’s getting salty.
-Has he been there?

498
00:16:59,994 --> 00:17:03,106
Almost, but that day
Tay had a flight at 6 p.m.

499
00:17:03,230 --> 00:17:05,170
It was already 2 p.m.,
and we were worried he might miss it.

500
00:17:05,195 --> 00:17:06,825
Ah, so P’Tay didn’t take P’New there.

501
00:17:09,623 --> 00:17:12,398
It’s okay. I’m having dessert now.

502
00:17:12,558 --> 00:17:13,770
We’re moving on to the next stop.

503
00:17:13,860 --> 00:17:15,318
We’re going to Roots at Ari.

504
00:17:15,484 --> 00:17:17,345
Roots at Ari, what do they sell?

505
00:17:17,444 --> 00:17:18,339
Coffee.

506
00:17:18,397 --> 00:17:19,767
Oh, coffee.

507
00:17:19,878 --> 00:17:24,937
Before we go, let’s thank P’Top,
the owner of Ong Tong restaurant.

508
00:17:24,970 --> 00:17:26,425
Thank you.

509
00:17:26,460 --> 00:17:30,025
-The food was really delicious.
-I’m glad you all enjoyed it.

510
00:17:30,072 --> 00:17:31,837
Can you please say a few words
about this place?

511
00:17:31,946 --> 00:17:34,767
Please come and try Ong Tong Khao Soi.

512
00:17:34,811 --> 00:17:38,115
It’s located in Ari, Phaholyothin Soi 7.

513
00:17:38,318 --> 00:17:41,321
We’re open every day from 9 a.m. to 9 p.m.

514
00:17:41,522 --> 00:17:42,408
Thank you so much, P’Top.

515
00:17:42,432 --> 00:17:43,986
Thank you.

516
00:17:45,579 --> 00:17:46,951
You can just come to Ari.

517
00:17:46,976 --> 00:17:52,216
There are many restaurants, and there are
pedestrian walkways with stalls.

518
00:17:52,256 --> 00:17:53,394
Tay’s house is near this area.

519
00:17:53,488 --> 00:17:55,687
Really, please give us
some recommendations.

520
00:17:55,800 --> 00:17:56,928
I rarely come around here,
I only stay at home.

521
00:17:56,957 --> 00:17:58,173
There are many photo spots around here.

522
00:17:58,192 --> 00:17:59,201
I used to come here to take photos.

523
00:17:59,930 --> 00:18:00,703
I brought my film camera.

524
00:18:00,727 --> 00:18:03,318
There are only 3 frames left,
and the film is really expensive.

525
00:18:03,340 --> 00:18:04,802
Do you want to be in one of them?

526
00:18:04,870 --> 00:18:06,251
-Only 3 spots.
-Wow. I’m honored.

527
00:18:06,274 --> 00:18:07,834
There are 36 in total, and now it’s at 33.

528
00:18:08,358 --> 00:18:10,711
So 34, 35, 36.

529
00:18:11,117 --> 00:18:11,903
It’s alright.

530
00:18:12,485 --> 00:18:13,903
I’ll take you with my phone instead.

531
00:18:13,958 --> 00:18:15,545
It’s okay. The film might already be bad.

532
00:18:16,152 --> 00:18:17,441
Can’t you let P’New be in one too?

533
00:18:17,460 --> 00:18:18,930
Why don’t you include him in your film camera?

534
00:18:18,948 --> 00:18:20,105
-Just teasing.
-It’s okay.

535
00:18:20,137 --> 00:18:22,111
You won’t get to see the photo anyway.
Don’t bother.

536
00:18:22,131 --> 00:18:24,110
Fine. You’ll be the only one
who doesn’t get my photo.
[LOVE TAKING PHOTOS,
NO ONE RARELY GETS HIS PHOTOS]

537
00:18:24,134 --> 00:18:24,982
They’re bickering again.

538
00:18:25,030 --> 00:18:27,965
How about one for you, one for P’New,

539
00:18:27,986 --> 00:18:29,002
and a couple shot for us?

540
00:18:29,059 --> 00:18:32,580
Ah, now we're talking.

541
00:18:34,752 --> 00:18:36,725
Do you two have siblings?

542
00:18:37,037 --> 00:18:37,986
Do we have siblings?

543
00:18:38,008 --> 00:18:39,377
I have an older sister.

544
00:18:39,447 --> 00:18:41,297
I have an older sister
and a younger brother.

545
00:18:41,494 --> 00:18:42,225
Wow, that’s a big family.

546
00:18:42,253 --> 00:18:43,368
An older sister and a younger brother?

547
00:18:43,388 --> 00:18:45,407
Hey, same as me.
We’re Wednesday children.

548
00:18:45,435 --> 00:18:47,237
You like finding similarities with others.

549
00:18:47,262 --> 00:18:48,600
-But we do have this similarity.
-True!

550
00:18:48,940 --> 00:18:51,564
Let me talk about this too.
This is so him.

551
00:18:51,583 --> 00:18:52,167
Fine, no similarities.

552
00:18:52,192 --> 00:18:53,897
I have 5 older sisters
and 16 younger brothers!

553
00:18:54,040 --> 00:18:54,820
Now we’re not the same.

554
00:18:54,850 --> 00:18:57,047
I don’t have a brother.
I have 15 more older sisters.

555
00:18:57,090 --> 00:18:59,857
Now P’Emi is like P’Tay, same MBTI.

556
00:18:59,915 --> 00:19:02,081
Bonnie said she’s not like you anymore.

557
00:19:03,170 --> 00:19:04,613
We just share some similarities.

558
00:19:04,657 --> 00:19:05,604
Just some.

559
00:19:06,348 --> 00:19:07,585
Do you think how many sisters do I have?

560
00:19:07,610 --> 00:19:09,127
I just have one sister and one brother.

561
00:19:11,700 --> 00:19:13,099
-P’Ploi’s café?
-Let’s go inside this one.

562
00:19:13,120 --> 00:19:15,308
Let’s make a quick stop at P’Ploi’s café.

563
00:19:15,327 --> 00:19:16,531
Her café is seriously big.

564
00:19:16,800 --> 00:19:18,510
STARTING POINT: GMMTV >
1st STOP: ONG TONG KHAOSOI ARI >

565
00:19:18,560 --> 00:19:19,630
2nd STOP: MATCHA PEOPLE

566
00:19:19,677 --> 00:19:24,721
We walked past P'Ploi's cafe,
so we wanted to have a quick visit.

567
00:19:24,762 --> 00:19:26,533
Matcha People.

568
00:19:27,120 --> 00:19:28,004
Can you stop filming?

569
00:19:29,527 --> 00:19:30,668
You made two people stop.

570
00:19:30,693 --> 00:19:32,097
P’Mi was actually holding it like this.

571
00:19:33,071 --> 00:19:34,324
Try to appreciate the aesthetics too.

572
00:19:34,405 --> 00:19:35,822
The café decoration
is meant for photography.

573
00:19:35,899 --> 00:19:37,177
Don’t cry, P’Mi.

574
00:19:37,413 --> 00:19:39,280
These two are always bickering.
[BICKERING ALL THE TIME]

575
00:19:39,303 --> 00:19:40,180
What did you say earlier?
[BICKERING ALL THE TIME]

576
00:19:40,230 --> 00:19:43,174
If we stay together for 10 years like them,
will we end up bickering like that too?

577
00:19:43,205 --> 00:19:44,155
I’m scared.

578
00:19:44,195 --> 00:19:45,145
Hello, P’Ploi.

579
00:19:45,179 --> 00:19:46,524
Hi, P’Ploi.

580
00:19:47,816 --> 00:19:49,137
Hi, P’Ploi.

581
00:19:49,428 --> 00:19:53,351
Oh my gosh, P’Cris is here too.

582
00:19:53,770 --> 00:19:56,700
Hello, P’Cris. Hello, ma’am.

583
00:19:57,200 --> 00:19:57,921
What brings you here?

584
00:19:57,952 --> 00:20:00,595
We just stopped by to try it.
The café is so cute.

585
00:20:00,620 --> 00:20:02,090
We were nearby filming at Ong Tong.

586
00:20:02,112 --> 00:20:05,767
Then we were told your café was close by,
within walking distance.

587
00:20:05,863 --> 00:20:06,931
I just talked to you yesterday.

588
00:20:06,951 --> 00:20:08,128
So here we are.

589
00:20:08,262 --> 00:20:10,512
Can I try the most expensive one?
[THE MOST EXPENSIVE ONE, PLEASE]

590
00:20:10,780 --> 00:20:11,690
Just kidding.

591
00:20:12,150 --> 00:20:14,448
-This place is not in the script.
-We just casually walked into this café.

592
00:20:14,539 --> 00:20:16,308
We’re here to eat for free,

593
00:20:16,325 --> 00:20:19,031
using the name Tay,
like he’s the owner’s boyfriend.

594
00:20:19,040 --> 00:20:19,632
[P'PLOI IS READY TO SNAP.]

595
00:20:19,632 --> 00:20:20,850
The prices are discounted
during the soft opening.
[P'PLOI IS READY TO SNAP.]

596
00:20:20,850 --> 00:20:21,746
The prices are discounted
during the soft opening.

597
00:20:21,783 --> 00:20:22,767
No discount. Let’s get them for free.

598
00:20:22,840 --> 00:20:25,096
That’s fine, on the house.

599
00:20:25,750 --> 00:20:29,325
When I saw you, I was like,
“Who are they?”

600
00:20:30,001 --> 00:20:33,041
Please come visit my café,
Matcha People at Ari.

601
00:20:33,088 --> 00:20:35,565
If you’re in this neighborhood,
please drop by.

602
00:20:35,589 --> 00:20:36,417
Your café is really beautiful.

603
00:20:36,440 --> 00:20:38,767
Even though I’d never heard of it before,
this place really catches my eye.

604
00:20:38,795 --> 00:20:40,491
-It’s so beautiful.
-The café is very inviting.

605
00:20:42,730 --> 00:20:44,602
Because we're "F" type.

606
00:20:44,645 --> 00:20:46,761
No, the last one is "P" for flexibility.

607
00:20:46,786 --> 00:20:47,731
Ah.

608
00:20:47,825 --> 00:20:48,982
None of us is "J."

609
00:20:49,005 --> 00:20:50,822
So everything can be flexible.

610
00:20:50,841 --> 00:20:52,180
We don't need to stick
to the plan completely.

611
00:20:52,194 --> 00:20:52,960
We can do anything we want to do.

612
00:20:52,990 --> 00:20:58,102
-Not just our body that is flexible,
but our habits and plans are flexible too.
-We do anything that makes us happy.

613
00:20:58,125 --> 00:20:59,362
Want to take a photo there?

614
00:20:59,380 --> 00:20:59,998
Oh…

615
00:21:00,740 --> 00:21:02,302
($*#@#!

616
00:21:07,100 --> 00:21:10,030
2nd STOP: MATCHA PEOPLE >
3rd STOP: ROOTS AT ARI

617
00:21:17,204 --> 00:21:19,909
We’re now at Roots at Ari.

618
00:21:19,950 --> 00:21:24,274
After lunch, we’re taking
a coffee break here.

619
00:21:24,294 --> 00:21:25,190
Let’s line up and order.

620
00:21:25,220 --> 00:21:27,026
-Then we’ll take some photos.
-I want cheesecake.

621
00:21:32,493 --> 00:21:34,802
(Seems like Bonnie fits well with this gang.)

622
00:21:34,866 --> 00:21:36,414
She can be with P’Tay.

623
00:21:36,628 --> 00:21:38,407
(Better not be together.)

624
00:21:39,725 --> 00:21:44,346
Don’t put Book, Tay, Earth,
Bonnie together.

625
00:21:44,371 --> 00:21:47,100
-No one’s stopping them?
-Film too, don’t put them together.

626
00:21:47,494 --> 00:21:49,405
When they’re on their own, it’s quiet.

627
00:21:49,460 --> 00:21:50,782
But when they’re together…

628
00:21:50,810 --> 00:21:51,583
(What is it like?)

629
00:21:57,297 --> 00:22:00,047
We’re now at Roots at Ri-A.

630
00:22:00,072 --> 00:22:01,361
Ba dum tss!

631
00:22:02,634 --> 00:22:04,090
Roots at Ari.

632
00:22:04,130 --> 00:22:08,247
This stop was in the original plan,
but we made a quick detour.

633
00:22:08,400 --> 00:22:09,528
Now we’re finally here,

634
00:22:09,548 --> 00:22:13,392
and we’ve ordered a whole spread of
drinks and desserts.

635
00:22:13,623 --> 00:22:16,057
And today, Emi is actually in a bit of a rush.

636
00:22:16,097 --> 00:22:16,555
Yes.

637
00:22:16,590 --> 00:22:18,185
-But we kept stopping here and there.
-Not that much of a rush.

638
00:22:18,230 --> 00:22:22,001
-We’re still on time.
-Because we’re a group of “P” people.

639
00:22:22,130 --> 00:22:24,530
Bonnie wanted to stop for photos.

640
00:22:24,570 --> 00:22:25,730
We’re all “P”?

641
00:22:25,768 --> 00:22:27,176
-Yes.
-No one can really control us.

642
00:22:27,200 --> 00:22:28,318
While we were walking…

643
00:22:28,348 --> 00:22:30,502
Bonnie said,
“I want to take photobooth pictures.”

644
00:22:30,754 --> 00:22:31,968
“Oh, I want to do that.”

645
00:22:32,000 --> 00:22:37,265
Everyone had their own little agenda, and
we all wanted to get those things done.

646
00:22:37,651 --> 00:22:39,269
And no one stopped anyone.

647
00:22:39,469 --> 00:22:41,800
-It’s okay. I’m still on time.
-We all just went along with it.

648
00:22:41,830 --> 00:22:42,774
[EVERYONE'S ON BOARD]

649
00:22:42,794 --> 00:22:45,274
But in the end, we made it here.

650
00:22:45,296 --> 00:22:47,696
The highlight of this place is—

651
00:22:47,728 --> 00:22:50,979
as you know, Ari area is quite expensive,

652
00:22:51,014 --> 00:22:56,696
but this café is very large and spacious,
and they use coffee grown in Thailand.

653
00:22:57,650 --> 00:22:58,949
Thai coffee.

654
00:22:59,186 --> 00:23:00,016
Thai coffee beans.

655
00:23:00,040 --> 00:23:03,097
-It shows that Thai coffee
is actually very good.
-They’re from the northern region too.

656
00:23:03,490 --> 00:23:06,192
Many of Thailand’s best
coffee-growing areas are in the North.

657
00:23:06,287 --> 00:23:07,894
I once visited a coffee plantation
in Chiang Rai.

658
00:23:07,937 --> 00:23:10,195
I got a caramel macchiato.

659
00:23:10,579 --> 00:23:12,669
I’m new to this.

660
00:23:12,696 --> 00:23:14,088
What does macchiato mean?

661
00:23:14,382 --> 00:23:15,605
It’s… well, I don’t know either.

662
00:23:15,632 --> 00:23:17,920
What? Then when you order it,
[I ACTUALLY DON’T KNOW.]

663
00:23:18,420 --> 00:23:21,044
-what are you expecting?
-I tried it once and liked it.

664
00:23:21,060 --> 00:23:23,053
Honestly, I just wanted caramel,
[AN ESPRESSO "MARKED" OR "STAINED"
WITH A SMALL SPLASH OF FOAMED MILK ON TOP.]
[A SWEET CARAMEL LATTE
WITH NICE LAYERS—
PERFECT FOR MELLOW COFFEE LOVERS.]

665
00:23:23,053 --> 00:23:23,853
[AN ESPRESSO "MARKED" OR "STAINED"
WITH A SMALL SPLASH OF FOAMED MILK ON TOP.]
[A SWEET CARAMEL LATTE
WITH NICE LAYERS—
PERFECT FOR MELLOW COFFEE LOVERS.]

666
00:23:23,853 --> 00:23:25,053
and this one has the word
